    {
      "id": "beacon-is-a-connection-not-a-packet",
      "title": "Six call-backs are a beacon; six segments of one connection are not",
      "rationale": "A beacon is a connection repeated on a metronome. tshark reports a capture packet by packet and Zeek reports the same capture connection by connection, so without the ephemeral source port every SYN, ACK and data segment counted as its own call-back: the mean interval collapsed toward zero, the jitter exploded, and a real beacon went undetected on any capture richer than one packet per flow. The mirror error is just as costly \u2014 a single bulk transfer whose segments happen to be evenly spaced must never be reported as command-and-control. Both flows here have the same cadence; only the number of connections tells them apart.",
